{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/7saaab","slideIndex":7,"text":"0:45. I used synthetic runs to verify that location tracking, turf ownership and the leaderboard worked together. Four demo accounts generated six runs, five owned turfs and twelve chat messages. User1 can open the bell on the map to review notifications. The captured screen shows friend-request alerts. Individual alerts can be marked read, and there is also a Mark All Read action.\nScreenshot: User1 on the iPhone 17e simulator, notifications.png."}
